    "title": "Drew Allar talks preparation as Penn State starts Big Ten play - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Alton Northup Allie Berube ,\n4 hours ago\nCENTRE COUNTY, Pa. (WHTM) — On the biggest stage, you need your biggest players to shine. There is no player who’s more crucial to Penn State’s success than quarterback Drew Allar.\nThe senior quarterback came into the season as a potential first-round draft pick. Now, the outside world is asking for him to prove it this week against his first ranked opponent of the season in Oregon.\nThrough three games, Allar has 64.8% completion percentage with four passing touchdowns and an interception. The offense is clearly still evolving as the Nittany Lions start Big Ten play.\nOn paper, it’s a rematch of the Big Ten championship game — a 45-37 loss for Penn State last season.\nAllar’s last performance against Oregon came in that championship game. He went 20-for-39, 226 passing yards, four total touchdowns and two interceptions.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WETM - MyTwinTiers.com.",
